{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792254126,"nonce":"4NSKiojIuIA3RNH3FoMYEskIh20=","message":"Root cause shared by chaos and raytrace: boxed_entry dunders (__add__, __mul__, __sub__, ...) always keep Object params, and their base bodies construct instances (GVector(self.x * other, ...), Vector/Point(self.x + other.x, ...)), so __init__ params and every field become Object. Plan: type boxed_entry dunders by their calls in view like other closed methods; open one (dynamic_methods) only when an operator/compare/subscript/call site with an Object operand, or a library route (sum, sorted, min, max, sort, index/count/remove, in), can dispatch to it; add reflected sites (2 * v -\u003e __rmul__) and comparison passed-types in operator_site/compare_site; the hooks already convert boxes via lowerer.dunder -\u003e coerce, which must stay checked (TypeError on a kind the analysis missed). The OTHER-escape alternative was refuted (38b017a).","files":null}]}